{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Moses went</b> — when he had finished all his words, then all those who stood before him departed — the little ones and the women, each man to his tent — and Scripture had no need to mention this, for it already said (above 29:9, 11): \"You stand this day, all of you, before HaShem your Elohim... to enter into the covenant of HaShem your Elohim,\" and after they entered the covenant they would depart from before him. And Scripture now says that Moses went from the camp of Levi to the camp of Israel to honor them, like one who wishes to take leave of his friend and comes to ask permission from him:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:57:04.881705160Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}